# ===== The Veil, task 5: kit changes (spec 4.2, D10, D14) =====
# Osiris side: goals/ARCANA_Status_Sigil.txt (a detonation adds Doubt) and the "Task 5" region of
# goals/ARCANA_Deceiver_Doubles.txt (Grand Deception's two stacks of Doubt). Details and reasons: 50_kit.md.
# Needs 10_doubt.patch (DOUBT_ADD_TECH, DOUBT_2/3), 20_doubles.patch (DOUBLE_OF_THE_VEIL_TECH, VEIL_LAYER_N,
# Arcana_Passive_VeilCap4/5) applied (they are, since apply session 1). 55_friends_upcast.patch goes with this one.
# Lists, progression rows, the ArcanaReact* resources, CardFamilies, CardDB and loca orphans are NOT here: see the
# "References for later tasks" table in 50_kit.md (Tasks 6, 7, 9, 10).

# ---------- Text ----------
# Existing handles, rewritten (each is used by exactly one stats entry).
# Malicious Whispers: a marked target also gains Doubt.
@loca h358611e4gab01gee5dg782ag87ac7ba30c60 Invade a creature's mind with malicious whispers, imposing <LSTag Tooltip="Disadvantage">Disadvantage</LSTag> on its next <LSTag Tooltip="AttackRoll">Attack Roll</LSTag>. A creature marked with your <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="SIGIL">Sigil</LSTag> also suffers <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="WHISPERED_PARANOIA">Paranoia</LSTag> and gains <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_1">Doubt</LSTag>.
# Paranoia (WHISPERED_PARANOIA): name its source on the status itself.
@loca h9fd48693g398dg74f3gf67dg102c1dbd8d83 Malicious Whispers on a creature marked with a Sigil. Can't take <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reactions</LSTag>.
# SIGIL: triggering the mark also inflicts Doubt (the Sigil goal applies it).
@loca h28e6ebc5g3632g32ddgd3d7ge688706a5796 The affected entity is marked by the Deceiver and takes additional [1] from their Arcane spells. Triggering the mark also inflicts <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_1">Doubt</LSTag>.
# Friends (the root's ExtraDescription): what the level-6 upcast adds (55_friends_upcast.patch).
@loca h9dd95e32gd1f4g9b57g9df7g7706c0b3938e This spell can be cast while you are <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="SILENCED">Silenced</LSTag>.<br><br>At level 6, it doesn't require <LSTag Tooltip="Concentration">Concentration</LSTag>, the target won't know you've enchanted them and it doesn't change in higher difficulty modes.

# New strings.
@loca VEILED_PRISON_NAME Veiled Prison
@loca VEILED_PRISON_DESC <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="VEILED_PRISON">Trap</LSTag> a creature behind a veil in its own mind, preventing movement, actions and reactions. Attacks from within [1] are always <LSTag Tooltip="CriticalHit">Critical Hits</LSTag>.
@loca VEILED_PRISON_EXTRA The creature can repeat the Saving Throw at the end of each of its turns.<br><br>A creature with 2 or more stacks of <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_2">Doubt</LSTag> has <LSTag Tooltip="Disadvantage">Disadvantage</LSTag> on every Saving Throw against this spell.
@loca VEILED_PRISON_STATUS_DESC Lost behind a veil in its own mind. Can't move, act or react. Automatically fails Strength and Dexterity <LSTag Tooltip="SavingThrow">Saving Throws</LSTag>, and attacks from within [1] are always <LSTag Tooltip="CriticalHit">Critical Hits</LSTag>.<br><br>At the end of each turn, can end the effect with a Wisdom Saving Throw, made with <LSTag Tooltip="Disadvantage">Disadvantage</LSTag> while it has 2 or more stacks of <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_2">Doubt</LSTag>.
@loca MARIONETTE_DOUBT_EXTRA A creature with 2 or more stacks of <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_2">Doubt</LSTag> has <LSTag Tooltip="Disadvantage">Disadvantage</LSTag> on the Saving Throw to resist this spell.
@loca GRAND_DECEPTION_NAME Grand Deception
@loca GRAND_DECEPTION_DESC Surround yourself with <LSTag Type="Passive" Tooltip="Arcana_Passive_TheVeil">Doubles</LSTag> until you reach your limit, and possibly fill the mind of every nearby enemy with <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DOUBT_2">Doubt</LSTag>.
@loca GRAND_DECEPTION_EXTRA Summons only the Doubles you are missing: you can keep 4, or 5 from level 12.<br><br>Enemies within [1] that fail a Wisdom <LSTag Tooltip="SavingThrow">Saving Throw</LSTag> gain 2 stacks of Doubt. A third stack leaves a creature <LSTag Type="Status" Tooltip="DELUDED">Deluded</LSTag>.
@loca GRAND_DECEPTION_TECH_NAME Grand Deception

# ---------- Malicious Whispers: a marked target also gains 1 Doubt ----------
# Same condition as the reaction lock, placed BEFORE the damage: the cantrip is an Arcane spell, so its own damage
# detonates the Sigil (SIGIL RemoveConditions) and the mark would be gone by the time a later IF looked for it.
# In SpellSuccess the source is the caster, so DOUBT_ADD_TECH lands in her name (no OnRemoveFunctors source issue).
@set Target_Arcana_Card_Spell_MaliciousWhispers SpellSuccess IF(HasStatus('SIGIL',context.Target,context.Source)):ApplyStatus(WHISPERED_PARANOIA,100,1);IF(HasStatus('SIGIL',context.Target,context.Source)):ApplyStatus(DOUBT_ADD_TECH,100,0);ApplyStatus(MALICIOUS_WHISPERS,100,1);DealDamage(LevelMapValue(D4Cantrip),Psychic,Magical);

# ---------- Marionette: Disadvantage on the save with 2+ Doubt (replaces AdvantageOnCharmed) ----------
# SavingThrow(ability, DC, advantage, disadvantage): vanilla passes `false` and an expression in 3rd/4th place
# (SavingThrow(Ability.Constitution, SourceSpellDC(),false,IsInorganic())). DOUBT_3 never lingers (the Doubt goal turns
# it into Deluded at once) but is listed so "2 or more" stays true to the text. _6 inherits SpellRoll through `using`.
@set Target_Arcana_Card_Spell_Marionette SpellRoll not SavingThrow(Ability.Wisdom,SourceSpellDC(),false,HasAnyStatus({'DOUBT_2','DOUBT_3'},{},{},context.Target))
@set Target_Arcana_Card_Spell_Marionette ExtraDescription {{MARIONETTE_DOUBT_EXTRA}}

