# ---------- New: Grand Deception (replaces Hostile Takeover) ----------
# A SHOUT, not the plan's "Target_" id: both halves are centred on her ("around you", "every enemy within 9 m"), the
# vanilla Radiance of the Dawn shape (Shout, AreaRadius 9, SpellRoll on Enemy() targets, a GROUND: functor in
# SpellProperties) and the Heroes' Feast shape (Shout + one GROUND:Summon at the caster). See 50_kit.md, decision 1.
#
# Summons: the Doubles' own path (template 8807d230 + DOUBLE_OF_THE_VEIL_TECH, cause = her, exactly Mirror Image's
# functor), so ARCANA_Deceiver_Doubles.txt registers, caps and forms each one. Only the MISSING ones are summoned:
# Summon number i is made when N + i <= cap, where N comes from her VEIL_LAYER_N (the goal keeps exactly one of
# VEIL_LAYER_1..5 on her = live Doubles, none at 0) and cap = 5 with Arcana_Passive_VeilCap5, 4 with
# Arcana_Passive_VeilCap4, else 3 (the same rule as QRY_ARCANA_Doubles_OverCap). The three OR terms nest, so each
# condition is "N <= cap - i" for whichever cap she has (checked by brute force: 4 cap cases x N 0..5, 0 mismatches).
# GROUND:IF(...):Summon(...) is vanilla (Find Familiar, Mage Hand). The conditions are read at the cast, before any of
# these Doubles registers.
# Doubt: a failed save applies GRAND_DECEPTION_TECH once; the Doubles goal turns it into two raises (Task 5 region).
# No Concentration; Long Rest (OncePerRest, as Marionette and Hostile Takeover); level 5 card; Unique = CardDB (Task 7).
